$WEATHER: Trial 2 NFT Lettuce - Greenhouse (natural daylight), University of Florida 2025-2026
! 2026-11-03: hours shifted to local standard time (EST, GMT-5). The logger clock was GMT-4, so every hourly row moved 1 h earlier (new hour h = former hour h+1); last hour 2026013-24 from the single 2026-01-14 00:05 reading. Crop grew in a greenhouse under natural daylight.
! 2026-11-03: PAR column added = measured PAR sensor (Indoor_Weather_Station.csv), hourly mean of 15 min readings, umol/m2/s x 0.0036 = mol/m2/h (9.27 mol/m2/d); same hour alignment as SRAD. Greenhouse daylight.
! 2026-11-02: hourly SRAD replaced with the measured Solar Radiation W/m2 column of Indoor_Weather_Station.csv (15 min readings averaged to hourly); replaces the PAR derived, raised and x1.5 values below.
! 2026-10-30: hourly SRAD converted from MJ/m2/h to W/m2 (W/m2 = MJ/m2/h x 1E6/3600), matching Oliveira et al. Flexible I/O; HR2DLY sums W/m2 x 0.0036 to MJ/m2/d.
! SRAD recomputed 2026-10-05 from the PAR column: SRAD (MJ/m2/h) = PAR (mol/m2/h) / (4.6 * 0.45)
! Cultivars: Salvius (Romaine), Casey (Butterhead), MC (Romaine)
! Transplant: 2025-12-15  Last harvest: 2026-01-13
! (superseded 2026-11-02) SRAD was derived from the PAR sensor (umol/m2/s) -> MJ/m2/h
! (superseded 2026-11-02) Conversion: SRAD = PAR / (4.6 * 0.45) * 3600/1e6
! Temperature from indoor weather station (15-min -> hourly avg), F->C
! Dew point calculated from RH and temperature
! Rain = 0 (controlled environment)
! 2026-10-06: PAR column removed and SRAD multiplied by 1.5 (SRAD = 1.5 x PAR / (4.6 x 0.45)) by user decision; photosynthetic light is then driven by SRAD.
! NOTE 2026-11-09: LAT/LONG set to the greenhouse at Live Oak, FL (30.301722 N, -82.899806 W, Individual Sensor Notes.docx); was Gainesville 29.638/-82.372. ELEV unchanged.
! NOTE 2026-11-09: night hours at the sensor floor (SRAD 0.6 W/m2 and PAR 1.2 umol/m2/s = 0.0043 mol/m2/h in the raw logger file) set to 0 = dark, so lit hours follow real daylight.
! NOTE 2026-11-10: SRAD and PAR multiplied by 1.05 (+5%), within the stated sensor accuracy (Onset S-LIA PAR and S-LIB solar: +/-5%, Individual Sensor Notes.docx).
